    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8ed557a0e6e3632bf64fdaa9f20421b677e04c85cfa7b2fb3d9c23f3aa5796c9",
      "text": "After breakfast, take a boat across Lake Titicaca to the Uros Islands.\n\nThe islands are built from totora reeds. The Aymara people who live here have preserved their traditional way of life, beliefs, customs and dress.\n\nTotora is used to build the islands and boats, and parts of the plant are also eaten. Fishing remains one of the islanders’ main occupations, and selling souvenirs to visitors provides extra income.\n\nAfter the tour, return to Puno and transfer to your hotel for the night.\n\nA visit to the Uros Islands shows you just how widely totora is used in daily life. The reeds form the islands themselves, are used to make boats and also provide food. Islanders continue their traditional occupations while welcoming visitors and selling handmade goods.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-113a0f7cb039-mwa5n0tf-qk0eyn5ma27",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      }
    },
